{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310534,"nonce":"KqgOlYRm1h3WPkQBAo8Jfxzph2M=","title":"FIXED ada97141 — the duplicate-release guard was blind to call-shaped frees, so a string header was freed twice. bench/eval now scores all ...","message":"**FOUND 2026-08-18 at `afd5cd95`** while building the NueGraph Stage 1 baseline\nharness. Pre-existing — NOT caused by that work.\n\n**REPRO (30s), from `nue/bench/eval`:**\n\n    rayzor run Main.hx --release --llvm --safety-warnings off -- \\\n      ~/models/qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf corpus.txt \\\n      --chunk 256 --max-chunks N\n\n| N | result |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | **exit 0**, `[chunk 1] pos=0 scored=255 ppl=22.8316` |\n| 2 | **exit 134**, chunk 1 printed, then dies |\n| 3 | exit 134, same |\n\n**exit 134 = 128+6 = SIGABRT, and it is SILENT** — no malloc message, no panic,\nno Haxe exception text, nothing after the chunk-1 line. Reproduces with the\npinned env AND with a bare default env, and on both the Q4_K_M and q5_0 0.5B\nmodels.\n\n**`gate.sh:50` sets `MAX_CHUNKS=\"${MAX_CHUNKS:-6}\"`, so the perplexity gate\nitself cannot run at HEAD.** Anything that shelled out to it and ignored the\nexit code has been passing vacuously.\n\n**WHY THE SHAPE MATTERS:** chunk 1 succeeds and chunk 2 aborts, i.e. the SECOND\niteration of the chunk loop. That is the signature of a value freed at the end\nof iteration 1 and reused in iteration 2 — the family of `255f9638` (a last use\nINSIDE A LOOP freed at that statement, because `should_drop_at_statement`\nignored the `in_loop` flag) and [[bugs_loop_body_class_alloc_never_freed]].\nSIGABRT rather than SIGSEGV points at the allocator detecting corruption\n(double free / bad pointer) rather than a null dereference.\n\n**SUPERSEDED — see LOCALISED below. (was: start at the chunk loop)** `nue/bench/eval/Main.hx` chunk loop — find what is allocated\nbefore the loop or in iteration 1 and freed at its end (KV cache reset, the\nscratch logits buffer, the token array slice). `RAYZOR_ALLOC_DEBUG=1` and\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]] before claiming anything leaks or\ndouble-frees.\n\n**IT BLOCKS NueGraph Stage 1 ARM B.** [[project_nuegraph_stage1_plan_ready]]\nuses bench/eval as the PREFILL oracle (teacher-forced, sampler-free,\ncontention-immune, required top1=100%). Arm A (generated text + dispatch\ncounters) is unaffected and is already PROVEN byte-identical across two HEAD\nruns. Until this is fixed, Stage 1 can only be gated on arm A — which does not\nexercise prefill.\n\n\n**LOCALISED 2026-08-18 — the crash is on the LOOP BACK EDGE, not in the body.**\nInstrumented every statement of the chunk loop with prints. Last output:\n\n    @loop-top pos=0 / @pre-slice n=256 / @post-slice len=256 / @post-reset\n    @post-forward / [chunk 1] ... / @pre-advance      \u003c-- then SIGABRT\n\nIteration 2 NEVER reaches `@loop-top`. Between `@pre-advance` and the next\niteration there is only `pos += n` (two Int locals — cannot fault) and the\nCOMPILER-INSERTED END-OF-BODY DROPS. So the fault is in the inserted drops.\n\n**FOUR HYPOTHESES TESTED AND ELIMINATED — do not re-test these:**\n1. `ids.slice(pos, pos+n)` returning an aliasing view → replaced with a manual\n   `for (wi in 0...n) window.push(ids[pos+wi])`. **Still aborts.**\n2. Explicit `logits.free()` racing an inserted drop → removed the in-loop\n   `free()`. **Still aborts.**\n3. `model.resetCache()` → removed. **Still aborts.**\n4. `ids` itself being dropped at its last in-loop use → added a use of `ids`\n   AFTER the loop so it is live past it. **Still aborts.**\n\nSo the double-freed value is a BODY-LOCAL — `window` (an Array, and arrays ARE\nhandled by insert_free) or the `logits` Tensor — dropped at the bottom of the\nbody in a way that is wrong on the second pass. Read\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]] first: loop-body NON-string/array\nallocs are explicitly SKIPPED, which is exactly why `window` (an array) is the\nprime suspect and `logits` is not.\n\n`RAYZOR_ALLOC_DEBUG=1` printed NOTHING on the release binary — it needs a debug\nbuild, so budget for that.\n\nA standalone two-`forwardIds` repro was attempted and is a DEAD END: it fails\nearlier with exit 133 (trap stub) for an unrelated reason. Reproduce inside\nbench/eval.\n\n\n**TWO OF MY OWN RESULTS ARE UNRELIABLE — READ BEFORE BUILDING ON THEM (2026-08-18).**\n\n1. **`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=InsertFree` still aborted — but that test is probably\n   VACUOUS.** Memory already records the flag as **BUNDLE-only**, and\n   `compilation.rs` contains no reference to the optimization manager, so the\n   source/JIT path this repro uses may never consult it. Do NOT conclude \"the\n   inserted drops are innocent\" from that run. Re-test by proving the flag has\n   an observable effect on this path FIRST (disable a pass whose absence is\n   visible), or bisect on a bundle instead.\n\n2. **The print-based localisation may be TRUNCATED BY STDOUT BUFFERING.** Output\n   was redirected to a file, so stdout is block-buffered, and SIGABRT does not\n   flush. `@pre-advance` being last does NOT prove execution stopped there —\n   iteration 2's prints could have executed and been lost in the buffer. Re-run\n   under a pty (`script -q /dev/null \u003ccmd\u003e`) or with an explicit flush before\n   trusting the cut point.\n\nSo the SOLID facts remain only: chunk 1 succeeds, chunk 2 aborts with a silent\nSIGABRT, reproducible with pinned and default env on two models; and the four\nsource-level hypotheses (slice aliasing, explicit free, resetCache, `ids`\ndropped) are eliminated because each was tested by EDITING THE SOURCE, which\nneeds no assumption about env flags or buffering.\n\n\n**PARTIALLY RESOLVED 2026-08-18 at `96b992fb`.** The `Sys.println(\"[chunk \" + …)`\nstatement that made this reproduce was one instance of\n[[bugs_string_concat_in_loop_double_free]], now fixed — every standalone\nloop-concat shape passes.\n\n**BUT bench/eval STILL DIES ENTERING CHUNK 2**, now `exit 133` (SIGTRAP) rather\nthan 134, with NO diagnostic and NO `W0020`. The crash report\n(`~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/rayzor-*.ips`) names:\n\n    _xzm_xzone_malloc_freelist_outlined   \u003c- libsystem_malloc\n    \u003cJIT frame\u003e -\u003e rayzor::run_file\n\ni.e. a CORRUPTED FREELIST discovered by a later malloc, not an invalid free.\nThat is a SECOND, independent corruption — and it is the same signature as the\nalready-fixed `139c4f5` (a MIR wrapper writing HaxeArray header fields at byte\noffsets where element indices were expected, leaving `elem_size = 0`). Reproduces\nwith AND without `--dump`, so it is not the dump array.\n\n**NEXT:** re-read `bugs_llama_chat_heap_corruption_confirmed` for the method that\ncaught `139c4f5`, and look for a header-field write in the tensor/quant MIR\nwrappers this path uses (`forwardIds` → prefill). `RAYZOR_HEAP_CHECK=1` exists\n(`runtime/src/heap_check.rs`) but currently has no `check_heap()` call sites on\nthis path — adding them around the forward is the documented bisection method.\n\n\n**RE-SCOPED 2026-08-19 at `eceff474`. bench/eval has AT LEAST TWO problems and\nneither is the string-concat bug.**\n\n1. **Restore-induced import resolution failures.** With the carried snapshot in\n   use, the run prints:\n\n       error[IMPORT]: nue.tokenizer.BPETokenizer — Cannot find type 'haxe.io' (217:17)\n       error[IMPORT]: nue.loader.GGUFTokenizer — Field 'spm' index not found for write\n\n   `haxe.io` is a PACKAGE, so a qualified name is being truncated. Set\n   `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1` (added `eceff474`) and the import errors\n   VANISH — proving they come from restoring the library rather than compiling\n   it. Same family as [[bugs_stdlib_artifacts_are_identical_restore_is_not]].\n   A minimal `haxe.io.Bytes.alloc` in an imported module does NOT reproduce it.\n\n2. **A SIGSEGV (exit 139) before chunk 1 even completes**, which survives with\n   the snapshot ignored and the import errors gone.\n\n**MY `96b992fb` FIX IS NOT THE CAUSE — A/B'd DIRECTLY.** Building the parent of\nthat commit and the commit itself, both with `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1`,\ngives **exit 139 / 0 chunks either way**. Do not blame the loop-temporary fix.\n\n**The chunk-2 framing in this file's title is now stale**: with a valid carried\nsnapshot the run no longer even reaches chunk 1, because failure mode (1)\narrives first. Reproduce with `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1` to work on (2)\nin isolation.\n\n**ONE UNEXPLAINED OBSERVATION, recorded rather than explained away:** the plain\nloop-concat repro failed ONCE with exit 133 on a cold run, then passed 10/10\ncold and 10/10 warm at the identical commit. Not reproducible; do not assume the\nloop-temporary path is fully deterministic until it is.\n\n\n**2026-08-19 SESSION 2 — MY FIXES ARE EXONERATED; THE HARNESS BUG IS ITS OWN,\nAND IT IS NONDETERMINISTIC. Read this before spending another day on it.**\n\n**TWO A/Bs, both showing NO effect from this session's work:**\n1. `96b992fb` (loop-temporary release) vs its parent, both with\n   `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1`: **exit 139 / 0 chunks either way.**\n2. String iteration-frees gated ON vs OFF (temporary `RZT_NO_ITER_STRING_FREE`),\n   3 cold runs each: **exit 139 / 0 chunks, 3/3, both arms.**\n\n**THE FAILURE MODE DRIFTS ACROSS BUILDS AND RUNS** — observed 134, 133, 139 and\n132, with 0 or 1 chunks completed, at commits that differ only in unrelated\ncode. Do NOT bisect this with single runs; a changed exit code is not evidence.\nOne earlier \"0 chunks + import errors\" reading was a WARM-CACHE artifact —\nalways `rm -rf .rayzor` before comparing.\n\n**AN EARLIER CLAIM IN THIS FILE WAS BACKWARDS.** With a properly cold cache:\n- carried snapshot IN USE → **chunk 1 completes**, dies on chunk 2, no import errors\n- `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1` → **0 chunks**, and the `haxe.io` import\n  errors APPEAR.\nSo compiling the library from source is what produces those import errors;\nrestoring it does not. That env var is therefore NOT a clean isolation tool here.\n\n**WHAT IS LOCALISED (with the snapshot in use, the reproducible arm):** markers\nvia `File.saveContent` put the death inside the SECOND `model.forwardIds(window)`\n— iteration 2 reaches `loop-top`, `post-slice`, `post-reset`, then dies. It is\nNOT capacity-related: chunk 64, 128 and 256 all die entering chunk 2.\n\n**ELIMINATED BY SOURCE EDITS (each re-tested, all still crash):** `window`\nhoisted out of the loop; `shp = logits.shape()` removed; `resetCache()` is\nimplicated only in that removing it avoids the crash by changing semantics (the\nrun then exits 1 on the row-count refusal, never doing a second full forward).\n\n**A STRAIGHT-LINE TWO-FORWARD PROBE PASSES** — `resetCache; forwardIds; score;\nresetCache; forwardIds` inside the same project, same model, prints ALL-OK. So\ntwo forwards plus scoring are not sufficient; the LOOP context is required.\n\n**NEXT TOOLING, not more bisection:** the previous heap hunt\n([[bugs_llama_chat_heap_corruption_confirmed]]) only cracked when it had\nsigaction+ucontext PC capture, `walk_fp_chain`, dladdr symbolisation and a\nper-PID JIT symbol map (commit 73564ab, \"preserved in tree\" — `walk_fp_chain` is\nin `runtime/src/profile.rs`, behind the `profile` feature). Turn that on and get\nthe JIT frame that issues the bad access; `lldb` CANNOT attach here (SIP), and\n`RAYZOR_ALLOC_DEBUG`/`RAYZOR_HEAP_CHECK` print nothing on this path.\n\n\n**FIXED 2026-08-19 in `ada97141`.** Root cause was NOT in this harness at all:\nthe free-insertion pass's duplicate guard matched only `IrInstruction::Free`, so\ncall-shaped releases (string/array/anon) were invisible and the repeatedly-run\npass stacked duplicates; a doubled `haxe_string_free` reclaims the header twice.\nSee [[bugs_release_guard_blind_to_call_shaped_frees]]. All 6 chunks now score,\nexit 0, 3/3 runs, positions=1530 — so the perplexity gate works again.\n\nFound by building the free-graph viewer, not by bisection. Every source-level\nhypothesis recorded above (slice aliasing, logits.free, resetCache, window, shp)\nwas correctly eliminated — the defect was never in Main.hx.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_bench_eval_aborts_on_second_chunk` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}